-- title:
--   Branch local rings at a crossing map into the two Gauss rings
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p\ge 5$ and a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak{X}$ for $p$, and let $X$ denote the base change of `DRModel.toBase p` along $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbb{Z}\to O$, where $O$ is a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, with fraction field $K$ and a ring homomorphism $\iota_K\colon K\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; assume $X$ integral, and let $x\in X$ and $\varphi\colon K(X)\to \overline{M}$ be a ring homomorphism into the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-base change `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * p)` of the full modular function field of level $p$ inside Laurent series. Two normalisations are imposed: $\varphi$ carries the germ at $x$ of the global section coming from $a\in O$ to the constant $\iota_K(a)$, and, the preimage under `pullback.fst` of the finite chart being nonempty, $\varphi$ carries the germ of each element $a$ of the finite chart algebra `chartAlgFin` to $a$ itself, read through the coefficientwise embedding of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ into Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Further data: a valuation subring $A\subset\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, an algebraically closed perfect field $k$ of characteristic $p$, a homomorphism $red\colon A\to k$, modular polynomial data for $p$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality of the two Hecke maps $\bar\alpha,\bar\beta$ at level $(1,p)$, a place specialisation $P$ with these data, a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$ with its two regular prolongations $R_1,R_2$, the hypothesis $\iota_K(a)\in A$ for all $a\in O$, and $to\kappa\colon O\to k$ with $to\kappa(a)=red(\iota_K(a))$. Let $w$ be a place of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1` lying in `ssPlaces p 1 k`, and assume there is $\hat\jmath\in O$ with $red(\iota_K(\hat\jmath))=w.\mathrm{evalAt}(j)$ together with an element $t$ of the maximal ideal of the stalk at $x$ with $\varphi(t)=j-\iota_K(\hat\jmath)$. Assume given a point $n$ of the fibre product of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compInf}\,k$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{compZero}\,k$ whose two images in $(\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).C$ are closed and both map to $x$ under the respective component map followed by `DRModel.baseChangeMap toκ`, and assume that the images $\xi_\infty,\xi_0$ of the generic point of $(\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{ratModel}\,k).C$ under these two composites both specialise to $x$. Finally let $t_F$ be a stalk element at $x$ with $\varphi(t_F)=j(q^p)-j^p$ whose image under the specialisation map into the stalk at $\xi_\infty$ lies in the maximal ideal, and assume $\varphi(s)$ lies in `R.nodeIntegers w` for every $s$ in the stalk at $x$, that is, in $R_1$, in $R_2$, and in every valuation ring $V$ of $\overline{M}$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V=w$. The conclusion is fourfold: $\varphi$ maps the stalk at $\xi_\infty$ into the valuation ring $R_1.\mathrm{integers}$ and its maximal ideal into the nonunits of that ring; likewise the stalk at $\xi_0$ into $R_2.\mathrm{integers}$ with maximal ideal into its nonunits; some element of the stalk at $\xi_\infty$ has $\varphi$-image `jFun 1 p` $=j$; and some element of the stalk at $\xi_0$ has $\varphi$-image `jQFun 1 p` $=j(q^p)$.
--
--   This is the oriented local identification at a supersingular crossing point of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_0(p)$ in characteristic $p$: the local rings at the generic points of the two components are carried by $\varphi$ into the two Gauss valuation rings of the prolongation tuple, the first component receiving $j$ and the second $j(q^p)$, with the orientation fixed by the vanishing of $j(q^p)-j^p$ along the first branch. It is used by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.nodeResidue_eq_zero_iff_and_ord_eq_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.nodeResidue_eq_zero_iff_and_ord_eq_of_specializes_of_mem_maximalIdeal), which compares residues and orders at the crossing.
